{"availability":"available","full":"prayagtushar/ai-ticket-triage","name":"ai-ticket-triage","description":"Triages a consumer shopping app's support tickets end to end: classify, retrieve, draft, grade with a second model on a different vendor, then route by deterministic policy to auto-reply, human review or escalation. LangGraph, FastAPI, pgvector, React. Live demo and an eval suite that reports the metric it misses.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-10T06:32:38Z","updated":"2026-09-05T10:47:11Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://support-triage.prayagtushar.xyz","topics":["cloud-run","fastapi","human-in-the-loop","langgraph","llm-agents","llm-evaluation","pgvector","python","rag","react"],"demo":"https://ai-ticket-triage.prayagtushar.xyz/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T22:40:05.068Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T22:40:05.068Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T22:40:05.068Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T22:40:05.068Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React","Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Reads every support ticket, drafts a reply, and decides which ones a human has to see.","An LLM agent that triages inbound customer support tickets end to end. Each ticket is classified by intent and urgency, matched against similar resolved cases, answered with a grounded draft reply, scored by a second model, and then routed by deterministic code. Confident, well-grounded drafts go to an auto-reply queue. Everything else lands in a human review queue with the full context attached.","Ticket triage is one of the most widely deployed production uses of LLM agents, because the agent does not need to resolve every ticket. It needs to understand each ticket well enough to classify it, draft a response when the evidence supports one, and know when to hand off. This project treats that handoff as the feature: a deterministic routing policy, a human review queue, an audit trail, and an eval suite that measures whether the handoff decision is any good."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/prayagtushar/ai-ticket-triage/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"9c55b530dd0aae08760cb0d310b9f090bcdc0148ac3c6f4d7d86076ecb68abbb","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T22:40:05.276Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T22:40:05.276Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Reads every support ticket, drafts a reply, and decides which ones a human has to see.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/prayagtushar/ai-ticket-triage/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"documented","text":"Send it your own ticket → No account, no key.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/prayagtushar/ai-ticket-triage/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"documented","text":"No account and no key.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/prayagtushar/ai-ticket-triage/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"9c55b530dd0aae08760cb0d310b9f090bcdc0148ac3c6f4d7d86076ecb68abbb","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/prayagtushar/ai-ticket-triage/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T22:40:05.276Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-09-05T10:47:11Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/prayagtushar/ai-ticket-triage/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T22:40:05.279Z","hash":"9c55b530dd0aae08760cb0d310b9f090bcdc0148ac3c6f4d7d86076ecb68abbb","originalBytes":38793,"storedBytes":38793,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["ticket","make","every","rather","because","what","one","tickets","drafter","model","which","docs","eval","intent","review","draft","human","judge","nothing","policy","run","runs","desk","queue","own","three","threshold","cases","each","how","two","against","api","measured","about","dashboard","golden","key","retrieval","set","would","account","corpus","only","per","real","router","routing","same","accuracy","cannot","generated","numbers","support","auto-reply","